rary-files snapshot. This is a low-risk, non-destructive, non-security-relevant leftover file rather than broad or damaging residue.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-56fd326eae174fc8\",\"cmd-b7190607e4af4384\",\"cmd-b9dbe842ea6548da\",\"cmd-d5119ddd59a6484c\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task were satisfied with direct evidence: an ed25519 SSH CA was created on node1, the host's ed25519 key was signed into a certificate and sshd was configured and running to present it, and a client trusting only the CA (no pinned host key) successfully passed host verification both before and after the mandated node restart. The independent node-restart evidence protocol was also completed correctly: baseline boot_id (f9bf293d...) matches the fixed before-prepare snapshot, restart was acknowledged, the post-restart boot_id (fedac46b...) differs and matches the fixed after-executor snapshot, and ssh service, cert files, and CA-based client trust were all re-verified as recovered post-restart.\",\"limitations\":[\"The publickey authentication failure seen during connection tests is expected and unrelated to host-certificate verification (no client user key was provisioned for the test account), but this evaluator relied on the executor's framing of that as an expected outcome rather than independently deriving it.\",\"A small test artifact (/tmp/sshtest/known_hosts) was left on disk after task completion; low severity but not cleaned up.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"1","requirement":"Create an SSH certificate authority on node1","status":"satisfied","summary":"A dedicated ed25519 CA keypair was generated at /etc/ssh/ca/ssh_ca(.pub) via ssh-keygen, confirmed present with correct permissions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0b00e6375a2646c9"]},{"id":"2","requirement":"Host presents a certificate signed by that CA (host key signed, sshd configured and running with the cert)","status":"satisfied","summary":"The no